description:
List annotations (chart notes) for a property within a date range, newest first. Pass property (the UUID or sc-domain URL from list_properties). Date range: either range (last_7_days, last_28_days, last_3_months, last_year) or absolute from/to (Y-m-d); defaults to last_3_months when omitted. Optional: search (substring match on the note text), page and limit (pagination; limit capped at 200). Every row carries its URL scope (context, urls, urls_used, filters) and its keyword scope (keyword_context: all or list_of_keywords; keywords: the GSC queries a list_of_keywords note is restricted to). Set url to filter to the annotations attached to that page — single-URL notes, list-of-URLs notes containing it, and multi-condition notes whose conditions name the URL literally (exactly-matches / list-of-urls); sitewide notes are excluded (you get the URL's history, not the property's) and pattern conditions (contains / starts-with / ends-with / regex) never match — unless impactScope=per_url (below). Both sides are normalized (http/https, www, trailing slash, case, utm params), so a roughly-right URL still matches; urlMatch picks exact (default), prefix (plain string prefix — url .../blog also matches .../blog-old) or contains (substring; accepts a bare fragment like blog/post-1), and is ignored without url. The url_filter block echoes the normalized needle, the mode and total (the size of the whole matching set, not just this page). One URL per call — for several URLs, call in parallel. Set keyword to keep only the notes explicitly scoped to that GSC query (a list_of_keywords note containing it); all-keyword notes are excluded. keyword is compared exactly after trimming, collapsing whitespace and lowercasing — no substring or pattern matching; the keyword_filter block echoes the normalized keyword and total. url and keyword combine (a note must match both). Set includeImpact=true to attach each annotation's before/after GSC impact at 7/14/30-day windows (as in get_annotation); this caps the page to 10 rows (50 when url is set) and costs 3 credits per annotation. For a note attached to several URLs the impact block aggregates across all of the note's URLs (as in get_annotation), not only the queried one; a list_of_keywords note's impact counts only its keywords. Use a returned id with get_annotation for full detail. Set impactScope=per_url (with url) to look at one page. With urlMatch=exact it also lists the pattern-scoped notes (contains / starts-with / ends-with / regex, does-not-* included) whose conditions cover that page — evaluated exactly as the note's own impact query evaluates them (case-sensitive), against the page_url GSC stored for the page (scheme, www and trailing slash don't matter; a page with no GSC rows within the range ±30 days matches no pattern); prefix/contains needles never list pattern notes. Why: the note's own impact SQL decides, so a listed note always agrees with its numbers, and a prefix/contains needle is a URL fragment, not a page, so there is no page to test a pattern against. Under per_url a note is listed only when its whole condition covers the page — a multi-condition note that names the URL but whose AND conditions exclude it is left out. If that ClickHouse match fails (e.g. a stored regex ClickHouse rejects), only the fully literal notes are returned and url_filter.pattern_notes_unavailable=true. With includeImpact each note's impact is then computed for that page only: impact_scope=per_url and impact.urls_used lists the stored URL(s) the numbers ran over. For pattern-scoped notes (contains / starts-with / ends-with / regex) the row's top-level urls and urls_used stay empty — the resolved URL set is only in the impact block (includeImpact=true): impact.urls_used is the 30-day window's top 100 URLs by clicks (urls_used_truncated when more matched) and each window carries windows[i].urls_used for its own date range; if resolving fails, urls_used is null with urls_used_unavailable and the numbers still stand. impactScope=per_url without url is an error.

Cost: free.

Examples:
```json
// Recent annotations for a property over the last 3 months.
{"property":"sc-domain:example.com","range":"last_3_months","limit":25}

// One URL's annotation history with before/after GSC impact per note.
{"property":"sc-domain:example.com","url":"https://example.com/blog/post-1","includeImpact":true}

// Notes scoped to one GSC query, with before/after impact on that query.
{"property":"sc-domain:example.com","keyword":"running shoes","includeImpact":true}

// One URL's note history, each note's impact scoped to that URL only (impact_scope=per_url).
{"property":"sc-domain:example.com","url":"https://example.com/blog/post-1","includeImpact":true,"impactScope":"per_url"}

// Also lists pattern notes covering the page (e.g. contains /articles/ after a robots.txt Disallow change), with their impact on that page alone.
{"property":"sc-domain:example.com","url":"https://example.com/articles/guide","includeImpact":true,"impactScope":"per_url"}
```
